{
  "info": {
    "name": "KairoX \u00b7 Inspection",
    "description": "Reject and rework, recorded against the stage RESPONSIBLE for the defect rather than the stage it was found at. The DM approves the re-walk.\n\nSETUP\n  1. Import the whole folder and SELECT the KairoX environment\n     (top-right). That is what shares one token across every\n     collection \u2014 a collection variable is visible only to the\n     collection that set it.\n  2. Run `user` \u2192 Login. Its test script stores `access_token` for\n     you; there is nothing to copy and paste.\n  3. Every request here inherits bearer auth from that token.\n\n`base_url` defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000.\n\nOptional query params are present but DISABLED, so each request runs\nas-is. File uploads are real form-data rows \u2014 click Select Files on\nthe `file` row. Generated from the app's own OpenAPI schema by\n`python scripts/make_postman_per_service.py` \u2014 re-run it after changing\nroutes rather than editing requests by hand.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Approve",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/inspections/{{inspection_id}}/approve",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "inspections",
            "{{inspection_id}}",
            "approve"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "inspection_id",
              "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "The DM agrees: the garment goes back (or is fixed where it stands).",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"note\": \"\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Decline",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/inspections/{{inspection_id}}/decline",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "inspections",
            "{{inspection_id}}",
            "decline"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "inspection_id",
              "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "The DM disagrees: the garment stays where it is and carries on.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"note\": \"\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "For Piece",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/inspections/pieces/{{piece_code}}",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "inspections",
            "pieces",
            "{{piece_code}}"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "piece_code",
              "value": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "One garment's inspection history, oldest first."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "List Inspections",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/inspections",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "inspections"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "status",
              "value": "",
              "description": "",
              "disabled": true
            },
            {
              "key": "limit",
              "value": "50",
              "description": "",
              "disabled": false
            },
            {
              "key": "offset",
              "value": "0",
              "description": "Rows to skip before returning `limit` rows.",
              "disabled": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Open rejections by default \u2014 the DM's queue.\n\n`offset` is here because a `limit` on its own is a CAP, not a pager: without\nit a caller can ask for the first 200 rows and has no way to ask for the\nnext 200."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Raise Inspection",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/inspections",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "inspections"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Raise a REJECT for the DM. A PASS may still be recorded deliberately.\n\n`verdict` IS OPTIONAL AND DEFAULTS TO REJECT \u2014 this screen is opened when a\ndefect has been found, so the smallest useful call is the piece and the stage\nit was seen at. `action` defaults to FIX (repair it where it stands); a REDO\nstill has to be asked for by name, with the stage to go back to.\n\nA PASS closes immediately \u2014 there is nothing to approve about a garment that\nis fine.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"piece_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n  \"piece_barcode\": \"\",\n  \"found_at_stage\": \"\",\n  \"verdict\": \"\",\n  \"action\": \"\",\n  \"return_to_stage\": \"\",\n  \"defect_type\": \"\",\n  \"responsible_employee_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n  \"responsible_stage\": \"\",\n  \"reason\": \"\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Responsibility",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/inspections/responsibility",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "inspections",
            "responsibility"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "employee_id",
              "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
              "description": "",
              "disabled": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Defects by the worker answerable for them.\n\nWORKMANSHIP ONLY. Product damage names nobody, so counting it here would put\na supplier's bad hide onto a person's record.\n\nDeclared BEFORE /pieces/{code} so the literal segment wins the match \u2014 FastAPI\nresolves in declaration order, and the other route would otherwise swallow\n\"responsibility\" as a piece code."
      },
      "response": []
    }
  ]
}